["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"A junior-high dropout who can&#x27;t draw won an Apple Design Award A self-taught outsider with a junior-high education who cannot draw built the first non-game app from China to win an Apple Design Award — by running into the wall again and again and never letting a feeling of ‘something&#x27;s off’ slide. Taste is not a gift; it is a habit built by long training. 知行小酒館 知行小酒館 E248 從 QQ 空間到蘋果設計大獎：一個非典型設計師的成長之路 Design Taste Product thinking Apple Design Award AI products Personal growth Flashcard Feature phone Quality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-zhixing-沒得選的野路子-如何撞出蘋果設計大獎/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/lusKQGmsgCgisjnGk6vQccpRzrpB.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"知\"><span class=\"dur\">1:18:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">知行小酒館</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>A junior-high dropout who can&#x27;t draw won an Apple Design Award</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A self-taught outsider with a junior-high education who cannot draw built the first non-game app from China to win an Apple Design Award — by running into the wall again and again and never letting a feeling of ‘something&#x27;s off’ slide. Taste is not a gift; it is a habit built by long training.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Taste</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Returning the Benin Bronzes: The Hard Question Is Not Whether, but to Whom Returning looted artifacts has become the correct position of the age, but with the Benin Bronzes ‘to whom’ is far harder to answer than ‘whether’: France and Germany are racing each other, Britain is playing dead, and three rival claimants inside Nigeria are fighting over them. Freakonomics Radio Freakonomics Radio Is a Museum Just a Trophy Case? (Update) Restitution Museums Colonial history Benin Bronzes Soft power Prosecution Benin Bronzes Deaccession Oba Punitive expedition\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-freakonomics-歸還貝寧青銅器不是終點-是道德選擇的開端/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/2be48404-a43c-4fa8-a32c-760a3216272e/fab1584e-8ea9-4efa-9650-5e595861b2cd/3000x3000/image.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">52:55</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Freakonomics Radio</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Returning the Benin Bronzes: The Hard Question Is Not Whether, but to Whom</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Returning looted artifacts has become the correct position of the age, but with the Benin Bronzes ‘to whom’ is far harder to answer than ‘whether’: France and Germany are racing each other, Britain is playing dead, and three rival claimants inside Nigeria are fighting over them.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Restitution</span><span class=\"tag\">Museums</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"China Shock 2.0: Not Cheap Goods, but Subsidies Crushing Global Industry Unlike 1.0, China Shock 2.0 is state capital turning to frontier manufacturing after the property crash, squeezing the world with subsidies and capacity — and AI may be the next battleground. The Ezra Klein Show Ezra Klein Show The China Shock 2.0 Trade War Industrial Policy EVs Rare Earths AI Competition Currency Manipulation three red lines reciprocal interdependence rare earths\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-ezra-中國衝擊2-0-國家資本正在改寫全球產業版圖/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/47913775-afcf-4643-935f-31f1dcc86cfb/6a0e5e15-04a3-47c8-9c50-2f2fe8e84437/3000x3000/teks-album-20art-3000px.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:05:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Ezra Klein Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>China Shock 2.0: Not Cheap Goods, but Subsidies Crushing Global Industry</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Unlike 1.0, China Shock 2.0 is state capital turning to frontier manufacturing after the property crash, squeezing the world with subsidies and capacity — and AI may be the next battleground.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trade War</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Memory Is a Painting, Not a Backup: Every Recollection Rewrites Itself Memory&#x27;s job is not to archive the past but to supply resources for the present and the future; every act of recall rebuilds the narrative, and collective memory is shaped further by power and emotion. The Gray Area with Sean Illing The Gray Area How memory changes you Neuroscience How memory works Collective memory Misinformation Self-identity episodic memory semantic memory schema cognitive dissonance collective memory highly superior autobiographical memory\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-grayarea-記憶不是備份而是一幅畫-每次回憶都在改寫自己/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/a3035ea0-fe19-11f0-8400-1fe1928680c7/image/09d3576515488959f432d219d5c7416b.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">59:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Gray Area with Sean Illing</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Memory Is a Painting, Not a Backup: Every Recollection Rewrites Itself</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Memory&#x27;s job is not to archive the past but to supply resources for the present and the future; every act of recall rebuilds the narrative, and collective memory is shaped further by power and emotion.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Neuroscience</span><span class=\"tag\">How memory works</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The AI Industry Spent Three Years Bracing for a Jobs Backlash; Data Centers Lit the Fuse AI companies spent three years preparing the communications playbook for a jobs shock, and the backlash broke out instead in the two places nobody had defended: data centers and child safety. Meanwhile, within two years, the bargaining power in local negotiations has flipped from communities courting companies to companies courting communities. Odd Lots Odd Lots Jasmine Sun on What the AI Industry Got Wrong About the Public Backlash Data centers AI politics Local finance Power and land Unions and labor Public backlash closed loop / open loop cooling exclusionary zoning reward hacking salience NIMBY\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-oddlots-ai-行業賭錯了民意爆點-不是失業-是數據中心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The AI Industry Spent Three Years Bracing for a Jobs Backlash; Data Centers Lit the Fuse</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI companies spent three years preparing the communications playbook for a jobs shock, and the backlash broke out instead in the two places nobody had defended: data centers and child safety. Meanwhile, within two years, the bargaining power in local negotiations has flipped from communities courting companies to companies courting communities.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Data centers</span><span class=\"tag\">AI politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Twenty Years of the Sun Disk Alone: The Pharaoh Struck From History For twenty years Akhenaten elevated the sun disk Aten above all other gods and moved his capital to a new city in the desert, trying to erase the old gods; after his death the religion was reversed, and both he and Nefertiti, who may have succeeded him, were struck from the lists of pharaohs. You&#x27;re Dead to Me You&#x27;re Dead to Me Akhenaten and Nefertiti: religious revolution in ancient Egypt Ancient Egypt Religious revolution Akhenaten Nefertiti Amarna Archaeology Aten Amarna Akhenaten Nefertiti\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-youdead-阿吞一神教的二十年-阿肯那頓與納芙蒂蒂被除名/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/400x400/p0p0czzs.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">58:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">You&#x27;re Dead to Me</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Twenty Years of the Sun Disk Alone: The Pharaoh Struck From History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">For twenty years Akhenaten elevated the sun disk Aten above all other gods and moved his capital to a new city in the desert, trying to erase the old gods; after his death the religion was reversed, and both he and Nefertiti, who may have succeeded him, were struck from the lists of pharaohs.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ancient Egypt</span><span class=\"tag\">Religious revolution</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"The DeLorean Case: Industrial Policy Should Never Bet on a Single Firm DeLorean built its factory on roughly $100 million in British government support, then slid into an $18 million fraud and an FBI cocaine sting. The real lesson of industrial policy is not whether to subsidize, but to keep several firms competing, use export markets as discipline, and never bet on one company. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales The DeLorean Saga: Fraud, Drugs and Marty McFly&#x27;s Car - with Business History Auto Industry Industrial Policy Government Subsidies Economies of Scale Corporate Fraud DeLorean gull-wing doors entrapment disciplined pluralism snowcat\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-cautionary-delorean-案-工業政策的核心是競爭紀律/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">49:04</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The DeLorean Case: Industrial Policy Should Never Bet on a Single Firm</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">DeLorean built its factory on roughly $100 million in British government support, then slid into an $18 million fraud and an FBI cocaine sting. The real lesson of industrial policy is not whether to subsidize, but to keep several firms competing, use export markets as discipline, and never bet on one company.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Auto Industry</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"The incinerator boom was not an environmental victory — it was a business the power tariff made pencil out A 2012 electricity tariff policy turned waste-to-energy from a money-loser into a profitable industry, and China built nearly 700 incineration plants in six years — only to end up with overcapacity and average utilization below 60%. Asianometry Asianometry China&#x27;s Fiery Incinerator Boom Vertical Industries Industrial Policy NIMBY Environmental Infrastructure Subsidy Economics Overcapacity Moving Grate Circulating Fluidized Bed BOT Decide-Announce-Defend\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-asianometry-六年七百座焚燒廠-補貼撐起的行業狂潮/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/AuIEBSb2xiE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The incinerator boom was not an environmental victory — it was a business the power tariff made pencil out</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A 2012 electricity tariff policy turned waste-to-energy from a money-loser into a profitable industry, and China built nearly 700 incineration plants in six years — only to end up with overcapacity and average utilization below 60%.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Vertical Industries</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Korean aesthetic medicine is cheap enough that losing the tax refund s