ding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Ancient Egypt had no queens: she could only be king, and was erased 20 years after her death</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Hatshepsut took power gradually from the position of regent, building royal authority through temples, trade and oracles; about 20 years after her death Thutmose III erased her on a large scale.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ancient Egypt</span><span class=\"tag\">Hatshepsut</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The real fix for alignment: humans have to keep faith with models first Bostrom&#x27;s core judgment: capability lockdown was never more than a temporary measure, and the real fix is alignment — which may require humans to start keeping their word to models now, because for a misaligned AI facing deletion, betting on a 5% chance of seizing power is the rational move. Odd Lots Odd Lots Nick Bostrom on What Happens if AI Solves All of Our Problems AI alignment Reward hacking Reinforcement learning Digital mind ethics Automation and distribution Longevity post-instrumental condition sandbagging reward hacking Goodharting moral patienthood simulation hypothesis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-oddlots-把-ai-關進盒子只是權宜-真解法是人先變得可信/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">55:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The real fix for alignment: humans have to keep faith with models first</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Bostrom&#x27;s core judgment: capability lockdown was never more than a temporary measure, and the real fix is alignment — which may require humans to start keeping their word to models now, because for a misaligned AI facing deletion, betting on a 5% chance of seizing power is the rational move.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI alignment</span><span class=\"tag\">Reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Korean Wave isn&#x27;t a cultural miracle — it&#x27;s a government-planned industrial counterattack From the rubble of the Korean War to BTS and Parasite, the Korean Wave looks like a cultural phenomenon. It is actually the route two generations of leaders, from Park Chung-hee to Kim Dae-jung, took to turn culture into an export industry using the instruments of the state. Throughline Throughline How Korean culture went global Korean Wave K-pop Industrial policy Cultural export Korean history Globalization Korean Wave Chaebol 3S policy Entrepreneurial state National humiliation Day\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-throughline-韓流不是文化奇蹟-是政府策劃的產業反攻/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2984x2984+0+0/resize/3000/quality/66/format/jpg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F48%2Fce%2Fb906c9c74361bf187754f9d6695e%2Fb1747544-3d16-4a7f-b5c6-28ab69610ca0.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Throughline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Korean Wave isn&#x27;t a cultural miracle — it&#x27;s a government-planned industrial counterattack</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From the rubble of the Korean War to BTS and Parasite, the Korean Wave looks like a cultural phenomenon. It is actually the route two generations of leaders, from Park Chung-hee to Kim Dae-jung, took to turn culture into an export industry using the instruments of the state.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Korean Wave</span><span class=\"tag\">K-pop</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Banks Reconcile by Phone, Not by System: One Wrong Ticket Can Cost Hundreds of Millions Who owes whom, and how much, between two institutions is often settled not by an automated reconciliation system but by phone calls, personal relationships, and the unspoken understanding that ‘we still have to do business together tomorrow’. Complex Systems Complex Systems Two banks can&#x27;t agree on fourth-grade math | Alex Elliott Clearing &amp; settlement Middle &amp; back office Prime brokerage Trading incidents Risk management Order flow MPID (Market Participant Identifier) Reg NMS / NBBO (national best bid and offer) Prime broker Golden record Payment for order flow Busting a trade\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-complexsys-兩家銀行連四年級數學都對不齊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/St-giYMCNRxOqSi0db5uiFmB2vKoxHbZlWUVWcLx51E/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS82OWRl/MDRmYjU0Mjk5MjNj/Yzk1OTE5MTQ2ZGJl/NjUxZi5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:03:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Banks Reconcile by Phone, Not by System: One Wrong Ticket Can Cost Hundreds of Millions</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Who owes whom, and how much, between two institutions is often settled not by an automated reconciliation system but by phone calls, personal relationships, and the unspoken understanding that ‘we still have to do business together tomorrow’.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Clearing &amp; settlement</span><span class=\"tag\">Middle &amp; back office</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Maya ballgame was ritual, not sport: the sacrificed-winner story is invented The Mesoamerican ballgame is humanity&#x27;s earliest rubber-ball team sport, but it was religious ritual first: the court re-staged the creation myth, and the people who could be killed were captives who lost a ritual re-enactment. The idea that the winners were sacrificed was made up later. The Ancients The Ancients The Maya Ballgame Maya civilization Mesoamerica Ballgame Religious ritual Archaeology Sports history Popol Vuh Mesoamerica Hero Twins yoke morning glory ball court\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-ancients-瑪雅球賽首先是宗教-贏家被獻祭是謊言/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f9e74b795a6299fd3b58/1786978898442-91a04567-af46-4b5d-9e78-085d63eb48cf.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Maya ballgame was ritual, not sport: the sacrificed-winner story is invented</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Mesoamerican ballgame is humanity&#x27;s earliest rubber-ball team sport, but it was religious ritual first: the court re-staged the creation myth, and the people who could be killed were captives who lost a ritual re-enactment. The idea that the winners were sacrificed was made up later.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Maya civilization</span><span class=\"tag\">Mesoamerica</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Burning tokens to stack up agents is a transitional strategy, not the endgame Silicon Valley is shifting from mindless token burning to careful accounting: a local open-source model can do real work on a dollar a day of electricity, yet when a genuinely hard problem shows up, a smarter model can still nail in one shot the answer a billion-token group chat could not argue its way to. Saving money and top-tier intelligence are not in conflict. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E249｜Token經濟轉點：OpenClaw、Hermes到本地自研的Agent進化之路 Token Economics Agent Engineering Open-Source Models Local Deployment B2B Startups Infrastructure Investing OpenClaw Agentic Loop FDE (Forward Deployed Engineer) Agent Native Jevons Paradox Gödel machine\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-sv101-堆agent燒token是過渡策略-不是終局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/f/f0f20376-8faf-4940-b920-84af6c734e2d/cover.jpg?v=6\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:27:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Burning tokens to stack up agents is a transitional strategy, not the endgame</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Silicon Valley is shifting from mindless token burning to careful accounting: a local open-source model can do real work on a dollar a day of electricity, yet when a genuinely hard problem shows up, a smarter model can still nail in one shot the answer a billion-token group chat could not argue its way to. Saving money and top-tier intelligence are not in conflict.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Token Economics</span><span class=\"tag\">Agent Engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Britain knew nothing about Northern Ireland, and hardline arson dragged Ireland toward civil war The Northern Ireland conflict was not simple sectarian hatred: Britain&#x27;s information vacuum, loyalist arson staged on purpose, and the civil rights movement&#x27;s genuine grievances amplified one another and together pulled Ireland toward civil war. The Rest Is History The Rest Is History 698. The Troubles: The Brink of Civil War (Part 2) Northern Ireland conflict civil rights movement British politics Irish history escalation of violence RUC / Royal Ulster Constabulary UVF / Ulster Volunteer Force NICRA / Northern Ireland Civil Rights Association B Specials\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-restishistory-英國的一無所知與強硬派的縱火把北愛推向內戰/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/00c0a118-2426-11ee-b258-73d331d0123b/image/db3295fcd9d3a7113e8000e931f0541d.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Rest Is History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>Britain knew nothing about Northern Ireland, and hardline arson dragged Ireland toward civil war</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Northern Ireland conflict was not simple sectarian hatred: Britain&#x27;s information vacuum, loyalist arson staged on purpose, and the civil rights movement&#x27;s genuine grievances amplified one another and together pulled Ireland toward civil war.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Northern Ireland conflict</span><span class=\"tag\">civil rights movement</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Adidas Bottoms Out: Reheating Old Hits Beats Superstar Collabs After nearly halving from its 2021 peak, Adidas engineered an earnings recovery by thawing out its retro sneakers, repairing its wholesale partners and holding inventory on a tight leash — but the share price rallied and then fell back again, showing that the sportswear cycle is really a game played between inventory and expectations. 商業就是這樣 商業就是這樣 Vol.271 阿迪達斯如何觸底反彈？ Adidas Sportswear Inventory management Share price cycles Retro sneakers Consumer goods Samba Months of supply Write-down provision Sub-two\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-bizthisway-阿迪達斯觸底反彈-炒冷飯比巨星聯名更穩/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://fdfs.xmcdn.com/storages/16ad-audiofreehighqps/A7/4F/GKwRIW4J7XyNAAdKlwLE2MK_.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"商\"><span class=\"dur\">28:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">商業就是這樣</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>Adidas Bottoms Out: Reheating Old Hits Beats Superstar Collabs</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">After nearly halving from its 2021 peak, Adidas engineered an earnings recovery by thawing out its retro sneakers, repairing its wholesale partners and holding inventory on a tight leash — but the share price rallied and then fell back again, showing that the sportswear cycle is really a game played between inventory and expectations.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Adidas</span><span class=\"tag\">Sportswear</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI Is Devaluing Code; an Engineer&#x27;s Moat Is Taste and Accountability Addy Osmani, who leads Chrome DevTools, argues that AI has devalued writing code and that an engineer&#x27;s real edge is taste and accountability — and warns against cognitive surrender, treating the AI&#x27;s answer as your own. The Pragmatic Engineer The Pragmatic Engineer From Chrome DevTools to AI Engineering, with Addy Osmani Chrome DevTools AI engineering Cognitive surrender Taste as moat Career change Frontend cognitive surrender alpha unbundling\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-pragmatic-ai-時代工程師的護城河是品味與問責/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/458709/post/211500766/c851926365279756d825ead10add906c.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:31:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Pragmatic Engineer</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>AI Is Devaluing Code; an Engineer&#x27;s Moat Is Taste and Accountability</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Addy Osmani, who leads Chrome DevTools, argues that AI has devalued writing code and that an engineer&#x27;s real edge is taste and accountability — and warns against cognitive surrender, treating the AI&#x27;s answer as your own.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Chrome DevTools</span><span class=\"tag\">AI engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"An AI Companion at $4M a Year: No Scripted Plot, Just Memory and Improvisation Tolon, the AI companion from Portola, threw out scripted plots and character sheets: memory is the character sheet, generation is improvisation, and the product is now at $4M in annualized revenue. This &quot;improv actor&quot; methodology and its mixed-model strategy are a second product path alongside ChatGPT. AI &amp; I AI &amp; I（Every） The AI Alien Companion App That&#x27;s Bringing In $4M a Year (Best of the Pod) AI Companions Improv Narrative Product Methodology LLM Applications Startups judge prompt lower seeds situations daemon\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-aiandi-ai-伴侶不做預設-記憶即角色-年入-400-萬美元/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/_unLmYM9CjKDeRXJOn7gFK3H6X2dny3KX6lhn0gohkg/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS8yNDM2/YzU4NDNmYTQxNTJh/MTEzYjE4YmJmYTg5/ODY1NS5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">AI &amp; I</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>An AI Companion at $4M a Year: No Scripted Plot, Just Memory and Improvisation</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Tolon, the AI companion from Portola, threw out scripted plots and character sheets: memory is the character sheet, generation is improvisation, and the product is now at $4M in annualized revenue. This &quot;improv actor&quot; methodology and its mixed-model strategy are a second product path alongside ChatGPT.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI Companions</span><span class=\"tag\">Improv Narrative</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"An AI Companion Made $4M in Four Weeks: 500ms More Latency and It Falls Apart Tolen, an AI alien companion, took ARR from $10,000 to $4M in four weeks — but add 500 milliseconds of latency and every metric collapses. Growth comes from viral video; retention comes from treating the AI as a narrative medium rather than a tool. Every Every $4M in 4 Weeks: How This AI Alien Companion App Took Off (Best of the Pod) AI companionship Viral growth Latency Model selection Narrative design Evals Big Five vibe prompting judge prompt character-driven computing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-every-4周破400萬美元-ai伴侶的爆紅與500ms陷阱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/ngTS4gUINVk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Every</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>An AI Companion Made $4M in Four Weeks: 500ms More Latency and It Falls Apart</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Tolen, an AI alien companion, took ARR from $10,000 to $4M in four weeks — but add 500 milliseconds of latency and every metric collapses. Growth comes from viral video; retention comes from treating the AI as a narrative medium rather than a tool.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI companionship</span><span class=\"tag\">Viral growth</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Illuminati Died of Infighting; the Conspiracy Theory Was Invented Later The Illuminati was an anti-clerical order founded in 1776 by a professor and five students, peaking at roughly two to three thousand members; it died of infighting and narcissism, and today&#x27;s conspiratorial image comes from later books and hoaxes. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class Adam Weishaupt and the Bavarian Illuminati Secret Societies Conspiracy Theories The Enlightenment Illuminati Organizational Management Information Spread Illuminati Minerval Covenant of Perfectibility Astroturfing Principia Discordia Illuminatus! Trilogy\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-stuffmissed-光照派從未統治世界-它連自己都管不好/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/programs/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/cfb428ef-eafc-44d0-9d09-ae2701747e6f/image.jpg?t=1749829805&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">43:04</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>The Illuminati Died of Infighting; the Conspiracy Theory Was Invented Later</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Illuminati was an anti-clerical order founded in 1776 by a professor and five students, peaking at roughly two to three thousand members; it died of infighting and narcissism, and today&#x27;s conspiratorial image comes from later books and hoaxes.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Secret Societies</span><span class=\"tag\">Conspiracy Theories</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Contrarianism Is Imitation Too: AI Will Weaken Social Contagion In an age of contagion, escape is not the cure. Burges bets that AI will actually weaken social contagion, and, drawing on Catholicism and on Cluny, argues that the real work is rebuilding intermediary institutions. Conversations with Tyler Conversations with Tyler Luke Burgis on Mimetic Desire, Catholicism, and the Age of Social Contagion Mimetic Theory AI Ethics Catholicism Social Contagion Institutional Design Gender Relations mimetic desire scapegoat mechanism achievement subject sprezzatura via negativa memento mori\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-19-tyler-ai-削弱社會傳染-反主流也是模仿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/9/5/a/1/95a1b2589a92292016c3140a3186d450/LukeBurgis-libsyn.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Conversations with Tyler</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0819</span></div>\n<h2>Contrarianism Is Imitation Too: AI Will Weaken Social Contagion</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In an age of contagion, escape is not the cure. Burges bets that AI will actually weaken social contagion, and, drawing on Catholicism and on Cluny, argues that the real work is rebuilding intermediary institutions.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Mimetic Theory</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Ethics</span>\n</div></div></a>"]